    "created_at": "2025-09-15T14:28:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-15T14:31:48Z",
    "body": "If I understand correctly, `Accept-Encoding` was restricted to the single value `identity` because [7 years ago 3.21% of web servers handled the request incorrectly](https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/747#issuecomment-393572169). However, I would also like to point out that this has removed the possibility of selectively reading files compressed with `deflate`, `zstd`, or `brotli`.\nHas anyone checked how many web servers respond incorrectly to `Accept-Encoding: deflate, identity` (like modern Firefox) or `Accept-Encoding: identity, deflate`?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
